            <ArticleTitle>Mrap2: an accessory protein linked to obesity.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>309-11</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.cmet.2013.08.016</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S1550-4131(13)00342-2</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Melanocortin receptors are critical modulators of energy balance and glucose homeostasis. Companion studies published in Science (Asai et al., 2013; Sebag et al., 2013) establish a role for melanocortin receptor accessory protein 2 (Mrap2) in regulating melanocortin receptor activity and in the development of obesity in zebrafish, rodents, and humans.</AbstractText>
